WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.338 --> 00:00:07.042
Hi! This is a quick tour of Portfolio Tracker.

2
00:00:07.062 --> 00:00:10.703
It's a desktop program for Windows and Mac that you buy once,

3
00:00:10.723 --> 00:00:12.131
with no subscription.

4
00:00:13.879 --> 00:00:17.507
For this tour, I've set up two demo accounts, a brokerage account

5
00:00:17.527 --> 00:00:22.635
and a Roth IRA. Up top, I'm viewing them together as one household.

6
00:00:22.668 --> 00:00:24.893
Let's walk through the main screens.

7
00:00:25.353 --> 00:00:27.169
We'll start on the Dashboard.

8
00:00:27.228 --> 00:00:29.479
The first row is the big picture.

9
00:00:29.524 --> 00:00:33.228
Your portfolio value, the change since the last close, and your

10
00:00:33.248 --> 00:00:35.116
return over the period you pick.

11
00:00:35.659 --> 00:00:37.935
These range buttons set that period.

12
00:00:37.955 --> 00:00:41.762
One year, five years, year to date, and so on.

13
00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:45.308
The grade and risk cards below follow the same window.

14
00:00:45.802 --> 00:00:47.708
Next come the income cards.

15
00:00:47.753 --> 00:00:50.948
Dividends so far this year, what you've been paid this month,

16
00:00:50.968 --> 00:00:54.175
and your estimated monthly and annual income.

17
00:00:54.195 --> 00:00:57.797
Yield on cost compares that income with what you paid.

18
00:00:58.302 --> 00:01:01.892
Portfolio Value Over Time charts your account history.

19
00:01:01.912 --> 00:01:04.940
It's rebuilt from your transactions, so you can see how you got

20
00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:05.719
here.

21
00:01:06.819 --> 00:01:10.357
Below that, the dividends expected this week, and your allocation

22
00:01:10.377 --> 00:01:13.355
by category, next to the targets you set.

23
00:01:13.413 --> 00:01:16.123
The Diff column shows where you're over or under.

24
00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:20.156
And at the bottom, every holding, with its cost basis, current

25
00:01:20.176 --> 00:01:24.110
value, dividends, yield, and total profit.

26
00:01:24.616 --> 00:01:26.561
Now the Dividend Calendar.

27
00:01:26.606 --> 00:01:30.451
Open the Portfolio menu, and choose Dividend Calendar.

28
00:01:32.272 --> 00:01:35.977
The month view puts each payment on the day the cash arrives.

29
00:01:36.035 --> 00:01:39.344
Days before today are payments you've already received.

30
00:01:39.377 --> 00:01:41.525
Later days are the ones still coming.

31
00:01:41.571 --> 00:01:45.620
The small icons tell you whether a date is confirmed, estimated,

32
00:01:45.754 --> 00:01:47.890
or matched to your imported history.

33
00:01:48.791 --> 00:01:52.407
Each day shows its total, and the top right shows the total for

34
00:01:52.426 --> 00:01:56.118
the month. That makes it easy to spot the lighter months.

35
00:01:56.646 --> 00:01:59.713
The Agenda view lists the same payments in order.

36
00:01:59.809 --> 00:02:03.514
For each one, you'll see the ex-dividend date, the amount per

37
00:02:03.534 --> 00:02:07.277
share, and whether the pay date is confirmed or estimated.

38
00:02:08.832 --> 00:02:13.110
Next, importing. Imports go into one account at a time, so I'll

39
00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:15.623
switch the selector to the brokerage account.

40
00:02:15.656 --> 00:02:18.200
Then open Admin, and choose Import.

41
00:02:22.406 --> 00:02:26.047
The Broker Import tab reads exports straight from your broker.

42
00:02:26.105 --> 00:02:30.626
Right now, that's Charles Schwab, E*TRADE, Fidelity, Robinhood,

43
00:02:30.646 --> 00:02:33.190
Shear Group, and Interactive Brokers.

44
00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:35.698
It works in three steps.

45
00:02:35.718 --> 00:02:39.741
Step 1, Positions, is a snapshot of what you own today.

46
00:02:39.799 --> 00:02:43.478
Step 2, Transactions, brings in your history, like dividends,

47
00:02:43.498 --> 00:02:45.915
DRIP, and buys and sells.

48
00:02:45.985 --> 00:02:50.315
Step 3, Refresh, updates prices and dividend data.

49
00:02:50.807 --> 00:02:54.422
What if your broker isn't on that list, or you keep your own spreadsheet?

50
00:02:54.455 --> 00:02:56.603
That's what the generic import is for.

51
00:02:56.661 --> 00:02:58.874
Start on the Generic Positions tab.

52
00:02:59.408 --> 00:03:03.559
Click Download Holdings Template to get a ready-made Excel file.

53
00:03:03.604 --> 00:03:07.500
Only two columns are required, Ticker and Shares.

54
00:03:07.533 --> 00:03:11.595
You can add price paid, dividend, frequency, and more, and market

55
00:03:11.615 --> 00:03:13.304
data is filled in for you.

56
00:03:13.837 --> 00:03:17.019
For your history, use Generic Transactions.

57
00:03:17.064 --> 00:03:20.794
Its template has one row per transaction, with a date, a type

58
00:03:20.814 --> 00:03:25.922
like buy, sell, or dividend, then the ticker, shares, price, and

59
00:03:25.942 --> 00:03:26.815
amount.

60
00:03:27.369 --> 00:03:30.079
Here's a small file I made in that format.

61
00:03:30.137 --> 00:03:32.477
I'll drop it in, and click Preview.

62
00:03:34.083 --> 00:03:37.482
The preview shows exactly what's in the file, before anything

63
00:03:37.502 --> 00:03:41.691
changes. And when you do import, any row that's already in your

64
00:03:41.711 --> 00:03:43.017
history is skipped.

65
00:03:43.076 --> 00:03:44.727
I won't import this one.

66
00:03:44.759 --> 00:03:46.742
It was just to show you the format.

67
00:03:50.325 --> 00:03:52.460
Now a couple of research tools.

68
00:03:52.519 --> 00:03:55.432
Open Analysis, then ETF Comparer.

69
00:03:56.696 --> 00:03:59.712
I'll add three popular dividend funds.

70
00:03:59.770 --> 00:04:03.092
SCHD, VYM, and JEPI.

71
00:04:03.625 --> 00:04:07.304
The chart shows total return, with dividends reinvested, over

72
00:04:07.324 --> 00:04:08.898
the period you choose.

73
00:04:08.931 --> 00:04:12.291
You can also switch to price only, to see the difference dividends

74
00:04:12.311 --> 00:04:13.044
make.

75
00:04:13.541 --> 00:04:15.090
Scroll down for more.

76
00:04:15.161 --> 00:04:19.375
There's yield on cost over time, each fund's distribution history,

77
00:04:19.395 --> 00:04:24.210
and a side by side table with yield, expense ratio, and returns.

78
00:04:25.791 --> 00:04:29.700
Further down, you'll find average returns over several periods,

79
00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:31.970
and each fund's top holdings.

80
00:04:33.238 --> 00:04:35.743
Right next to it is ETF Overlap.

81
00:04:35.789 --> 00:04:37.860
It answers a simple question.

82
00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:42.248
If I own both of these funds, how much am I really diversifying?

83
00:04:42.839 --> 00:04:46.429
I'll pick a popular pair, VOO and QQQ.

84
00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:52.036
The circle shows overlap by weight, not just shared tickers.

85
00:04:52.107 --> 00:04:55.812
Here, a big part of each fund sits in the same companies.

86
00:04:56.350 --> 00:04:59.991
The sector chart shows where each fund leans, and the table lists

87
00:05:00.011 --> 00:05:01.572
the shared holdings.

88
00:05:01.592 --> 00:05:05.208
When two funds overlap a lot, buying both can add more of the

89
00:05:05.228 --> 00:05:07.937
same risk, instead of spreading it out.

90
00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:11.300
Now, Cash Flow and Sustainability.

91
00:05:11.358 --> 00:05:13.226
It's in the Portfolio menu.

92
00:05:15.962 --> 00:05:18.786
This screen is also a full budgeting tool.

93
00:05:18.831 --> 00:05:23.008
You list your income and expenses once, with categories, due dates,

94
00:05:23.028 --> 00:05:24.883
and how often they repeat.

95
00:05:24.954 --> 00:05:28.276
Portfolio Tracker adds your dividend income for you.

96
00:05:28.784 --> 00:05:31.826
Adding an expense only takes a moment.

97
00:05:31.871 --> 00:05:35.869
I'll add a gym membership, thirty dollars a month, under Health,

98
00:05:35.889 --> 00:05:37.757
and click Add expense.

99
00:05:41.891 --> 00:05:44.192
The cards up top update right away.

100
00:05:44.238 --> 00:05:49.179
Expenses this month, portfolio income before and after tax, and

101
00:05:49.199 --> 00:05:52.636
what's left over. The green banner tells you whether your income

102
00:05:52.656 --> 00:05:54.498
covers this month's bills.

103
00:05:55.064 --> 00:05:57.595
Further down, there's a stress test.

104
00:05:57.653 --> 00:06:01.804
It runs bull, neutral, and bear markets over the years ahead,

105
00:06:01.850 --> 00:06:03.909
with and without your other income.

106
00:06:04.405 --> 00:06:08.823
In this demo, the tougher cases run short over twenty years, mostly

107
00:06:08.843 --> 00:06:11.783
because expenses keep growing with inflation.

108
00:06:11.815 --> 00:06:14.729
That's exactly the kind of thing you want to find out early.

109
00:06:15.234 --> 00:06:17.829
That brings us to Retirement Readiness.

110
00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:20.253
It's in the Portfolio menu, too.

111
00:06:22.604 --> 00:06:25.556
It uses your budget and your portfolios together.

112
00:06:25.614 --> 00:06:29.242
Monthly expenses and other income are pulled straight from the

113
00:06:29.262 --> 00:06:33.132
cash flow plan. Here, that's Social Security and a pension, about

114
00:06:33.152 --> 00:06:35.721
thirty six hundred a month before tax.

115
00:06:36.230 --> 00:06:38.136
Then you set your assumptions.

116
00:06:38.194 --> 00:06:42.039
I'll use a six percent yield in good markets, four and a half

117
00:06:42.059 --> 00:06:45.585
percent in a bear market, and fifteen thousand dollars of cash

118
00:06:45.605 --> 00:06:46.605
set aside.

119
00:06:48.335 --> 00:06:49.986
The cards show the result.

120
00:06:50.006 --> 00:06:53.060
What the portfolio needs to pay each month, the income it can

121
00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:56.836
produce in good and bad markets, and the gap to a safety buffer

122
00:06:56.856 --> 00:06:58.660
of three times that need.

123
00:06:59.176 --> 00:07:00.700
The badge sums it up.

124
00:07:00.745 --> 00:07:03.264
In this demo, it says Building.

125
00:07:03.322 --> 00:07:07.332
The portfolio covers the gap today, even in a bear market, but

126
00:07:07.352 --> 00:07:09.475
the full buffer isn't there yet.

127
00:07:09.508 --> 00:07:13.672
The chart and milestones below show how that changes over time.

128
00:07:14.217 --> 00:07:15.779
And that's the tour.

129
00:07:15.837 --> 00:07:19.784
Portfolio Tracker is a one-time purchase for Windows and Mac,

130
00:07:19.804 --> 00:07:21.838
and you can find it on Gumroad.

131
00:07:21.896 --> 00:07:23.228
Thanks for watching!

132
00:07:24.482 --> 00:07:26.719
For informational purposes only.

133
00:07:26.765 --> 00:07:28.832
Not financial advice.
